File Index

/normalizePluginModule.ts
Purpose: Normalizes plugin module structure and validates data types for consistent plugin handling. Spreads the raw module first so unlisted hooks pass through — a field-by-field copy once dropped `onAlias` and killed every plugin's alias commands (b825d70 → PR #160).

/normalizePluginModule.test.ts
Purpose: Pins the actions-array passthrough (valid array kept, non-array dropped to undefined, absent stays undefined) and onAlias passthrough, plus that every hook and an unknown future hook survive normalization.

/pluginHost.ts
Purpose: Manages plugin lifecycle, execution, and communication within the game client. Registration and syncInstalled are instance-preserving: a running plugin is never re-created just because the installed list changed. api.log/api.error stamp exactly one `[plugin:<id>]` prefix on each terminal line — plugins must not repeat their own id in the message. api.setHudWidget (optional on PluginRuntimeApi) publishes into the hudWidgetRegistry under the plugin's id; disable() clears every ALL_HUD_SLOT_IDS slot for that plugin unconditionally (the registry's ownership check makes it a no-op for slots it doesn't own). invokePluginAction returns 'ok' | 'no-handler' | 'error' (not a bare boolean) so callers (PluginConfigModal) can tell "no handler was found" apart from "a handler ran and threw" instead of flashing the same failure label for both. replaceEnabledPluginConfig sets a running plugin's config to {...defaults, ...overrides} (exactly what a reload gives it), whereas updateEnabledPluginConfig only MERGES a patch and so can never take a key away (a setting set back to its default, or a cleared optional field with no default, would linger): use replace for "this is the saved config", update for "this one change".

/pluginHost.test.ts
Purpose: Pins that a running plugin instance survives installed-list churn and re-registration — plugin modules are closures, so a silent rebuild loses in-flight state (this is what broke text-to-speech). Also covers api.setHudWidget: publish is owner-attributed, disable clears only the disabling plugin's own slots. invokePluginAction: 'ok' only when a registered handler actually ran, 'no-handler' with no throw when no handler/plugin is found, 'error' (distinct from 'no-handler') when a found handler throws.

/pluginConfigOverrides.ts
Purpose: What a plugin's saved config should hold: only the values that differ from the plugin's defaults, because a saved copy of a default freezes it and later default changes never reach that user (item 2026-10-17_plugin-config-save-freezes-defaults). Equality is strict and structural ON PURPOSE: no coercion ("5" is a stored override of 5), objects ignore key order, arrays do not. toOverrides never mutates its input (callers pass frozen getConfig() snapshots); pruneRecordOverrides returns the SAME array when nothing drops, so callers can skip a write. Tests: pluginConfigOverrides.test.ts, including a pass over every core plugin's own defaults.

/pluginConfigPersist.ts
Purpose: One-way event a running plugin uses to persist a config change it made ITSELF (a floating toggle button, not the config modal) — api.updateConfig is in-memory only and syncInstalled re-applies the saved userConfig over it, so an unpersisted self-toggle silently reverts. Sends a PATCH, never the whole runtime config (that would promote every default into an explicit saved value); MainContainer merges it onto the install record.

/pluginScriptRunner.ts
Purpose: Runs bundled plugin scripts as triggers, timers, or aliases within a runtime environment.

/registry.ts
Purpose: Registers and provides access to all core plugins for the game client.

shared/regexCache.ts: patterns are tried as case-insensitive regexes with a literal-substring fallback for ones that do not compile; never pass g/y flags (a cached RegExp with lastIndex state would skip matches). shared/memoLast.ts keeps ONE remembered argument, so two call sites that alternate need their own instance (text-to-speech has one parser each for include and exclude).
